{
  "summary": "Replaces the wallet's dual `mapWallet` and `wtxOrdered` transaction storage with a single `boost::multi_index_container` indexed by txid and insertion order. Replaces direct map lookups across RPC methods, wallet methods, and tests with calls to `GetWalletTx()` or explicit index views. Marks `CWalletTx::MarkDirty()` const so cached transaction amounts can be reset through const references returned by the multi-index container.",
  "problem": "The wallet must access transactions both by txid and by arrival/insertion order. Managing two separate containers required the secondary container (`wtxOrdered`) to store raw pointers into `mapWallet`, requiring manual synchronization between the two maps and risking dangling pointer bugs.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author PR description: 'allowing us to get rid of the 2 separate containers, and holding raw pointers to CWalletTx.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches transaction lookup and iteration across most wallet subsystems, wallet RPCs, and wallet unit/fuzz tests. Requires linking `Boost::headers` for `bitcoin-wallet` executable in CMake.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This PR replaces the wallet's dual mapWallet and wtxOrdered transaction containers with a single boost::multi_index_container indexed by txid and insertion order. Storing transactions across two separate maps previously required holding raw pointers into mapWallet and manually synchronizing mutations between them. The refactor updates internal wallet accessors, tests, and RPC endpoints to query the unified container or use GetWalletTx. It is an internal refactor with no reported behavior changes or prerequisites.",
